## The defaults I took

The PM order of 2026-11-10 gives the rule of the second exception. The prompt named the default: the
first exception try of the id and kind must cost 0 USD, and the second try of that pair is the last
one. I read the rule this way and wrote it in D15:

- the second try is allowed when the first exception try of that id and kind cost 0 USD;
- the second try is refused when the first exception try cost more than 0 USD;
- a third try of that id and kind is refused;
- the try of the second exception counts against the same 0.15 USD cap, because it shares the start
  time.

The prompt did not name the cost of a failed call. I used the cost of the `usage_cost` column, so a
network fault at 0 USD gives 0.

